cells:
  - kind: 1
    value: >
      # Tree density Agent — simplified


      This notebook defines only two database routines: one setup procedure and
      one Agent-callable calculation function. The calculation function runs
      setup itself, so the user never creates the results table or views
      manually.


      Prerequisites: the translated physical tables BOMEN_TREES and
      GEZOND_GREEN_NEIGHBOURHOOD already exist. Their creation is a separate
      source-loading workflow. This notebook does not drop existing density
      results or modify Ask Oracle APEX code.


      Run the cells in order. This tree dataset covers Den Haag (GM0518), which
      is used when no municipality is named. Other municipalities are rejected
      rather than reported with misleading zero-tree counts. Omitting the green
      threshold means all Den Haag neighbourhoods with geometry.
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: >
      ## 1. Setup procedure


      Creates TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS if absent. Creates or repairs BOMEN_TREES_V,
      GEZOND_GREEN_NEIGHBOURHOOD_V, and TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS_V only when needed.
      The views exclude SDO_GEOMETRY; the results table retains it for maps.
      Existing run rows are preserved.
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "DROP VIEW IF EXISTS TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS_V;\r

      DROP TABLE IF EXISTS TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      
      -- prepare_tree_density_storage creates TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS if absent and
      creates or 

      -- repairs three nonspatial views: BOMEN_TREES_V,
      GEZOND_GREEN_NEIGHBOURHOOD_V, and

      -- TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS_V. It requires the two source tables to exist; it
      does not 

      -- calculate density.




      CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE prepare_tree_density_storage AS
          v_count NUMBER;

          PROCEDURE ensure_nonspatial_view(p_table_name IN VARCHAR2) AS
              v_view_name VARCHAR2(128) := p_table_name || '_V';
              v_columns   VARCHAR2(32767);
              v_exists    NUMBER;
          BEGIN
              -- This local helper accepts only the three known tables.
              IF p_table_name NOT IN (
                  'BOMEN_TREES',
                  'GEZOND_GREEN_NEIGHBOURHOOD',
                  'TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS'
              ) THEN
                  RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20020, 'Unsupported view source.');
              END IF;

              SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_exists
              FROM user_tables
              WHERE table_name = p_table_name;

              IF v_exists = 0 THEN
                  RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20021,
                      'Required table is missing: ' || p_table_name);
              END IF;

              SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_exists
              FROM user_objects o
              WHERE o.object_name = v_view_name
                AND o.object_type = 'VIEW'
                AND o.status = 'VALID'
                AND NOT EXISTS (
                    SELECT 1
                    FROM user_tab_columns c
                    WHERE c.table_name = v_view_name
                      AND c.data_type = 'SDO_GEOMETRY'
                );

              IF v_exists > 0 THEN
                  RETURN;
              END IF;

              FOR c IN (
                  SELECT column_name
                  FROM user_tab_columns
                  WHERE table_name = p_table_name
                    AND NOT (
                        data_type = 'SDO_GEOMETRY'
                        AND data_type_owner = 'MDSYS'
                    )
                  ORDER BY column_id
              ) LOOP
                  IF v_columns IS NOT NULL THEN
                      v_columns := v_columns || ', ';
                  END IF;
                  v_columns := v_columns ||
                      't."' || REPLACE(c.column_name, '"', '""') || '"';
              END LOOP;

              IF v_columns IS NULL THEN
                  RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20022,
                      'No nonspatial columns: ' || p_table_name);
              END IF;

              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE
                  'CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW "' || v_view_name ||
                  '" AS SELECT ' || v_columns ||
                  ' FROM "' || p_table_name || '" t';
          END ensure_nonspatial_view;
      BEGIN
          -- The translated physical source tables must already exist.
          SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_count
          FROM user_tables
          WHERE table_name IN (
              'BOMEN_TREES', 'GEZOND_GREEN_NEIGHBOURHOOD'
          );

          IF v_count <> 2 THEN
              RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20023,
                  'Translated source tables are missing. Load them first.');
          END IF;

          SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_count
          FROM user_tables
          WHERE table_name = 'TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS';

          IF v_count = 0 THEN
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  CREATE TABLE TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS (
                      RUN_ID             VARCHAR2(32) NOT NULL,
                      NEIGHBOURHOOD_ID   NUMBER NOT NULL,
                      NEIGHBORHOOD_NAME  VARCHAR2(254 CHAR),
                      MUNICIPALITY_CODE  VARCHAR2(30 CHAR),
                      DATA_YEAR          VARCHAR2(30 CHAR),
                      GREEN_THRESHOLD    NUMBER,
                      GREEN_PERCENTAGE   NUMBER,
                      TREE_COUNT         NUMBER,
                      AREA_SQ_KM         NUMBER,
                      TREES_PER_SQ_KM    NUMBER,
                      GEOMETRY           MDSYS.SDO_GEOMETRY,
                      CREATED_AT         TIMESTAMP DEFAULT SYSTIMESTAMP,
                      CONSTRAINT TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS_PK
                          PRIMARY KEY (RUN_ID, NEIGHBOURHOOD_ID)
                  )~';
          END IF;

          ensure_nonspatial_view('BOMEN_TREES');
          ensure_nonspatial_view('GEZOND_GREEN_NEIGHBOURHOOD');
          ensure_nonspatial_view('TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS');
      END prepare_tree_density_storage;

      /
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: >
      ## 2. Calculation function


      This is the only function exposed as an Agent tool. It first calls the
      setup procedure, then inserts one saved run and returns measured values
      plus the five highest-density neighbourhoods. Dynamic SQL for the result
      table lets the function remain compilable when that table has been dropped
      and needs recreation.
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- tree_density_agent_fn is the calculation tool. It calls the setup
      procedure, \r

      -- counts trees inside each qualifying neighbourhood polygon, calculates
      trees per km², \r

      -- and saves the results and polygons in TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS under a new
      RUN_ID. \r

      -- It returns a JSON summary; p_map_scope tells the app which saved
      polygons to display.\r

      \r

      -- RUN_ID is the unique ID for one calculation. It keeps results from
      different questions—such \r

      -- as under 30% and under 50% green area—separate, so the answer and map
      use the correct saved\r

      --  polygons.\r

      \r

      CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION tree_density_agent_fn (\r

      \    p_municipality    IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,\r

      \    p_green_threshold IN NUMBER   DEFAULT NULL,\r

      \    p_map_scope       IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL\r

      ) RETURN CLOB AS\r

      \    PRAGMA AUTONOMOUS_TRANSACTION;\r

      \r

      \    v_requested       VARCHAR2(254);\r

      \    v_code            VARCHAR2(30);\r

      \    v_matches         NUMBER;\r

      \    v_year            VARCHAR2(30);\r

      \    v_run_id          VARCHAR2(32);\r

      \    v_count           NUMBER;\r

      \    v_total_trees     NUMBER;\r

      \    v_highest_density NUMBER;\r

      \    v_top_five        CLOB;\r

      \    v_result          CLOB;\r

      \    v_map_scope       VARCHAR2(10);\r

      BEGIN\r

      \    -- The function creates missing result storage before calculating.\r

      \    prepare_tree_density_storage;\r

      \r

      \    v_map_scope := NVL(UPPER(TRIM(p_map_scope)), 'NONE');\r

      \r

      \    IF v_map_scope NOT IN ('TOP_1', 'TOP_5', 'ALL', 'NONE') THEN\r

      \        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20035, 'Invalid map scope.');\r

      \    END IF;\r

      \r

      \    IF p_green_threshold IS NOT NULL AND\r

      \       (p_green_threshold < 0 OR p_green_threshold > 100) THEN\r

      \        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20030,\r

      \            'Green-area threshold must be between 0 and 100.');\r

      \    END IF;\r

      \r

      \    v_requested := UPPER(TRIM(p_municipality));\r

      \r

      \    IF v_requested IS NOT NULL AND v_requested NOT IN (\r

      \        'GM0518', 'DEN HAAG', 'THE HAGUE',\r

      \        'S-GRAVENHAGE', '''S-GRAVENHAGE'\r

      \    ) THEN\r

      \        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20031,\r

      \            'This tree-density dataset supports Den Haag only.');\r

      \    END IF;\r

      \r

      \    v_code := 'GM0518';\r

      \r

      \    SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_matches\r

      \    FROM GEZOND_GREEN_NEIGHBOURHOOD\r

      \    WHERE MUNICIPALITY_CODE = v_code;\r

      \r

      \    IF v_matches = 0 THEN\r

      \        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20034,\r

      \            'Den Haag neighbourhoods are missing from the source
      table.');\r

      \    END IF;\r

      \r

      \    SELECT MAX(YEAR) INTO v_year\r

      \    FROM GEZOND_GREEN_NEIGHBOURHOOD\r

      \    WHERE MUNICIPALITY_CODE = v_code;\r

      \r

      \    IF v_year IS NULL THEN\r

      \        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20032,\r

      \            'No neighbourhood year for municipality ' || v_code);\r

      \    END IF;\r

      \r

      \    v_run_id := RAWTOHEX(SYS_GUID());\r

      \r

      \    -- Save every qualifying polygon for this run. The map scope below\r

      \    -- controls which saved rows GET_RESPONSE will display.\r

      \    EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~\r

      \        INSERT INTO TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS (\r

      \            RUN_ID, NEIGHBOURHOOD_ID, NEIGHBORHOOD_NAME,\r

      \            MUNICIPALITY_CODE, DATA_YEAR, GREEN_THRESHOLD,\r

      \            GREEN_PERCENTAGE, TREE_COUNT, AREA_SQ_KM,\r

      \            TREES_PER_SQ_KM, GEOMETRY\r

      \        )\r

      \        WITH eligible AS (\r

      \            SELECT n.ID,\r

      \                   n.NEIGHBORHOOD_NAME,\r

      \                   n.MUNICIPALITY_CODE,\r

      \                   n.YEAR,\r

      \                   n.PERCENTAGE,\r

      \                   n.GEOMETRY,\r

      \                   SDO_GEOM.SDO_AREA(\r

      \                       n.GEOMETRY, 0.05, 'unit=SQ_KM'\r

      \                   ) AS AREA_SQ_KM\r

      \            FROM GEZOND_GREEN_NEIGHBOURHOOD n\r

      \            WHERE n.MUNICIPALITY_CODE = :municipality_code\r

      \              AND n.YEAR = :data_year\r

      \              AND (:threshold_null IS NULL OR\r

      \                   n.PERCENTAGE < :threshold_filter)\r

      \              AND n.GEOMETRY IS NOT NULL\r

      \        ), counted AS (\r

      \            SELECT e.*,\r

      \                   (SELECT COUNT(*)\r

      \                    FROM BOMEN_TREES b\r

      \                    WHERE SDO_RELATE(\r

      \                        b.GEOMETRY, e.GEOMETRY, 'mask=INSIDE'\r

      \                    ) = 'TRUE') AS TREE_COUNT\r

      \            FROM eligible e\r

      \        )\r

      \        SELECT :run_id,\r

      \               ID, NEIGHBORHOOD_NAME, MUNICIPALITY_CODE,\r

      \               YEAR, :saved_threshold, PERCENTAGE,\r

      \               TREE_COUNT, AREA_SQ_KM,\r

      \               CASE WHEN AREA_SQ_KM > 0\r

      \                    THEN ROUND(TREE_COUNT / AREA_SQ_KM, 2)\r

      \               END,\r

      \               GEOMETRY\r

      \        FROM counted~'\r

      \    USING v_code, v_year, p_green_threshold,\r

      \          p_green_threshold, v_run_id, p_green_threshold;\r

      \r

      \    v_count := SQL%ROWCOUNT;\r

      \r

      \    IF v_count = 0 THEN\r

      \        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20033,\r

      \            'No neighbourhoods matched this request.');\r

      \    END IF;\r

      \r

      \    EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~\r

      \        SELECT SUM(TREE_COUNT), MAX(TREES_PER_SQ_KM)\r

      \        FROM TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS\r

      \        WHERE RUN_ID = :run_id~'\r

      \    INTO v_total_trees, v_highest_density\r

      \    USING v_run_id;\r

      \r

      \    EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~\r

      \        SELECT JSON_ARRAYAGG(\r

      \                   JSON_OBJECT(\r

      \                       'name' VALUE NEIGHBORHOOD_NAME,\r

      \                       'trees_per_sq_km' VALUE TREES_PER_SQ_KM\r

      \                       RETURNING CLOB\r

      \                   )\r

      \                   ORDER BY TREES_PER_SQ_KM DESC\r

      \                   RETURNING CLOB\r

      \               )\r

      \        FROM (\r

      \            SELECT NEIGHBORHOOD_NAME, TREES_PER_SQ_KM\r

      \            FROM TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS\r

      \            WHERE RUN_ID = :run_id\r

      \            ORDER BY TREES_PER_SQ_KM DESC, NEIGHBOURHOOD_ID\r

      \            FETCH FIRST 5 ROWS ONLY\r

      \        )~'\r

      \    INTO v_top_five\r

      \    USING v_run_id;\r

      \r

      \    SELECT JSON_OBJECT(\r

      \               'status' VALUE 'success',\r

      \               'run_id' VALUE v_run_id,\r

      \               'map_scope' VALUE v_map_scope,\r

      \               'municipality_code' VALUE v_code,\r

      \               'data_year' VALUE v_year,\r

      \               'green_threshold' VALUE p_green_threshold,\r

      \               'neighbourhood_count' VALUE v_count,\r

      \               'total_trees' VALUE v_total_trees,\r

      \               'highest_density' VALUE v_highest_density,\r

      \               'top_five' VALUE v_top_five FORMAT JSON\r

      \               RETURNING CLOB\r

      \           )\r

      \    INTO v_result\r

      \    FROM dual;\r

      \r

      \    COMMIT;\r

      \    RETURN v_result;\r

      EXCEPTION\r

      \    WHEN OTHERS THEN\r

      \        ROLLBACK;\r

      \        RAISE;\r

      END tree_density_agent_fn;\r

      /"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: >
      ## 3. Agent definitions


      One tool invokes the calculation function. The function itself guarantees
      setup before calculation. Reuse the existing team name so Ask Oracle does
      not gain another density team. The supervisor routes density questions to
      the worker. The task lists only questions supported by the returned
      metrics; it must not claim that the map rendered.
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      -- Replace only this density team's metadata. Saved result rows are
      untouched.

      BEGIN
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.DROP_TEAM(
              'TREE_DENSITY_MAP_TEAM', force => TRUE);
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.DROP_AGENT(
              'TREE_DENSITY_SUPERVISOR', force => TRUE);
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.DROP_AGENT(
              'TREE_DENSITY_AGENT', force => TRUE);
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.DROP_TASK(
              'TREE_DENSITY_TASK', force => TRUE);
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.DROP_TOOL(
              'TREE_DENSITY_TOOL', force => TRUE);
      END;

      /
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "\r

      \r

      -- tool_inputs 're input parameters of tree_density_agent_fn, passed in by
      TREE_DENSITY_TOOL\r

      BEGIN\r

      \    DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.DROP_TOOL(\r

      \        'TREE_DENSITY_TOOL', force => TRUE\r

      \    );\r

      \r

      \    DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.CREATE_TOOL(\r

      \        tool_name => 'TREE_DENSITY_TOOL',\r

      \        attributes => q'~{\r

      \            \"function\": \"TREE_DENSITY_AGENT_FN\",\r

      \            \"instruction\": \"Calculate and save Den Haag neighbourhood
      tree density. Return the measured JSON result, including RUN_ID and
      MAP_SCOPE. Use TOP_1 for the single highest-density neighbourhood, TOP_5
      for the five highest, ALL when the user asks to show every qualifying
      neighbourhood, and NONE for a counts-only question.\",\r

      \            \"tool_inputs\": [\r

      \                {\r

      \                    \"name\": \"p_municipality\",\r

      \                    \"description\": \"Optional Den Haag name or GM0518;
      null defaults to Den Haag.\"\r

      \                },\r

      \                {\r

      \                    \"name\": \"p_green_threshold\",\r

      \                    \"description\": \"Optional green-area percentage
      threshold; null means no threshold.\"\r

      \                },\r

      \                {\r

      \                    \"name\": \"p_map_scope\",\r

      \                    \"description\": \"TOP_1, TOP_5, ALL, or NONE. Select
      according to the user's requested map result.\"\r

      \                }\r

      \            ]\r

      \        }~',\r

      \        description => 'Saves density polygons and returns the run ID and
      requested map scope.'\r

      \    );\r

      END;\r

      /"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "BEGIN\r

      \    DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.DROP_TASK(\r

      \        'TREE_DENSITY_TASK', force => TRUE\r

      \    );\r

      END;\r

      /\r

      BEGIN\r

      \    DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.CREATE_TASK(\r

      \        task_name => 'TREE_DENSITY_TASK',\r

      \        attributes =>\r

      \            '{\"instruction\":\"' ||\r

      \            q'|Answer the user's tree-density question: {query}\\n\\n|'
      ||\r

      \            q'|1. Call TREE_DENSITY_TOOL exactly once.\\n|' ||\r

      \            q'|2. Pass the municipality when given; otherwise pass null.
      Den Haag/GM0518 is the default.\\n|' ||\r

      \            q'|3. Pass the stated green-area percentage; otherwise pass
      null. Never assume 30%.\\n|' ||\r

      \            q'|4. Set p_map_scope to match the neighbourhoods named in
      the answer. Use ALL only when asked for every qualifying neighbourhood,
      and NONE for counts-only questions. Say when a requested selection is
      unsupported.\\n|' ||\r

      \            q'|5. Report only measured values and neighbourhood names
      returned by the tool.\\n|' ||\r

      \            q'|6. The percentage filters green area, not tree
      counts.\\n|' ||\r

      \            q'|7. Do not claim the browser map rendered unless the
      application confirms it.\\n|' ||\r

      \            q'|8. This dataset supports Den Haag only.|' ||\r

      \            '\",\"tools\":[\"TREE_DENSITY_TOOL\"]}',\r

      \        description => 'Answers measured Den Haag tree-density
      questions.'\r

      \    );\r

      END;\r

      /"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      BEGIN
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.CREATE_AGENT(
              agent_name => 'TREE_DENSITY_AGENT',
              attributes => q'~{
                  "profile_name": "OCI_GROK_4_3_BOMEN_BURRT_PROFILE",
                  "role": "You are the density worker. Follow TREE_DENSITY_TASK, call its tool once, and report only measured results."
              }~',
              description => 'Tree-density worker.'
          );

          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.CREATE_AGENT(
              agent_name => 'TREE_DENSITY_SUPERVISOR',
              attributes => q'~{
                  "profile_name": "OCI_GROK_4_3_BOMEN_BURRT_PROFILE",
                  "role": "You supervise the Den Haag tree-density team. For a greeting, briefly describe the supported density questions with examples. For a density request, delegate once to TREE_DENSITY_AGENT and return its measured answer. Do not invent a result or claim a map rendered. If the request is outside tree density, explain this team's scope.",
                  "supervisor": true
              }~',
              description => 'Routes supported density requests to the worker.'
          );
      END;

      /
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      BEGIN
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.CREATE_TEAM(
              team_name => 'TREE_DENSITY_MAP_TEAM',
              attributes => q'~{
                  "process": "sequential",
                  "supervisor_agent": "TREE_DENSITY_SUPERVISOR",
                  "agents": [
                      {
                          "name": "TREE_DENSITY_AGENT",
                          "task": "TREE_DENSITY_TASK"
                      }
                  ]
              }~',
              description => 'One supervised tree-density team; no second map team.'
          );
      END;

      /
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: >
      ## 4. Tests


      Run these one at a time. They append new results; they do not drop the
      results table. The first tool test should return JSON with a new RUN_ID, a
      neighbourhood count, and top_five names. For Den Haag under 30% green
      area, the earlier notebook observed 33 neighbourhoods, but live data
      should be checked rather than assumed. The team test uses a new
      conversation. Map rendering is not tested by this notebook.
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: |+
      -- Verify the tool and its automatic setup without manually creating tables/views.
      SELECT DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.RUN_TOOL(
                 tool_name => 'TREE_DENSITY_TOOL',
                 input     => '{"P_MUNICIPALITY":null,"P_GREEN_THRESHOLD":30}'
             ) AS tool_result
      FROM dual;
      -- TOOL_RESULT                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 
      -- --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
      -- {"status":"success","result":"{\"status\":\"success\",\"run_id\":\"5EE510F02FE53AFFE063AB11000A1BBD\",\"municipality_code\":\"GM0518\",\"data_year\":\"2022\",\"green_threshold\":30,\"neighbourhood_count\":33,\"total_trees\":25186,\"highest_density\":3084.74,\"top_five\":[{\"name\":\"Transvaalkwartier-Midden\",\"trees_per_sq_km\":3084.74},{\"name\":\"Kerketuinen en Zichtenburg\",\"trees_per_sq_km\":2558.09},{\"name\":\"Transvaalkwartier-Noord\",\"trees_per_sq_km\":2306.46},{\"name\":\"Laakkwartier-Oost\",\"trees_per_sq_km\":2254.1},{\"name\":\"Schildersbuurt-Noord\",\"trees_per_sq_km\":2184.5}]}"} 

    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: |
      -- Check that the Agent-created objects are valid.
      SELECT object_name, object_type, status
      FROM user_objects
      WHERE object_name IN (
          'TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS', 'TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS_V',
          'BOMEN_TREES_V', 'GEZOND_GREEN_NEIGHBOURHOOD_V'
      )
      ORDER BY object_name;

      -- OBJECT_NAME                  OBJECT_TYPE STATUS 
      -- ---------------------------- ----------- ------ 
      -- BOMEN_TREES_V                VIEW        VALID  
      -- GEZOND_GREEN_NEIGHBOURHOOD_V VIEW        VALID  
      -- TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS         TABLE       VALID  
      -- TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS_V       VIEW        VALID  


      -- Elapsed: 00:00:00.002
      -- 4 rows selected.
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: |
      -- Check the latest saved run, including geometry retained in the table.
      SELECT RUN_ID,
             COUNT(*) AS NEIGHBOURHOODS,
             COUNT(DISTINCT NEIGHBOURHOOD_ID) AS UNIQUE_NEIGHBOURHOODS,
             SUM(CASE WHEN GEOMETRY IS NOT NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS POLYGONS,
             MIN(TREES_PER_SQ_KM) AS MIN_DENSITY,
             MAX(TREES_PER_SQ_KM) AS MAX_DENSITY
      FROM TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS
      WHERE RUN_ID = (
          SELECT RUN_ID
          FROM TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS
          GROUP BY RUN_ID
          ORDER BY MAX(CREATED_AT) DESC
          FETCH FIRST 1 ROW ONLY
      )
      GROUP BY RUN_ID;

      -- RUN_ID                           NEIGHBOURHOODS UNIQUE_NEIGHBOURHOODS POLYGONS MIN_DENSITY MAX_DENSITY 
      -- -------------------------------- -------------- --------------------- -------- ----------- ----------- 
      -- 5EE510F02FE53AFFE063AB11000A1BBD             33                    33       33       88.59     3084.74 


      -- Elapsed: 00:00:00.012
      -- 1 rows selected.
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      -- End-to-end team test. The question does not require a municipality
      code.

      DECLARE
          v_conversation_id VARCHAR2(4000);
          v_response        CLOB;
      BEGIN
          v_conversation_id := DBMS_CLOUD_AI.CREATE_CONVERSATION();

          v_response := DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.RUN_TEAM(
              team_name   => 'TREE_DENSITY_MAP_TEAM',
              user_prompt => 'Which five Den Haag neighbourhoods have the highest tree density despite having less than 30% green area?',
              params      => '{"conversation_id":"' || v_conversation_id || '"}'
          );

          DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(DBMS_LOB.SUBSTR(v_response, 4000, 1));
      END;

      /
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: >
      ## Questions this agent can answer


      - Which Den Haag neighbourhood has the highest tree density (trees per
      km2)?

      - Which five Den Haag neighbourhoods have the highest tree density despite
      having less than 30% green area? (You can choose another percentage.)

      - How many neighbourhoods meet that green-area threshold, and how many
      trees are in them?

      -


      The percentage filters green area, not tree counts. The agent uses the Den
      Haag dataset (GM0518) when no municipality code is supplied. It saves
      density polygons in TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS, but this notebook alone does not
      display them in the Ask Oracle map.
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: >
      ## Next step


      This notebook does not create a K-means model. Once the density team is
      verified, OML can read one RUN_ID from TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS_V. The stored
      GEOMETRY remains in TREE_DENSITY_RESULTS for later map integration. Do not
      drop the old BUILD_TREE_DENSITY_LAYER or GET_TREE_DENSITY_MAP_LAYER
      routines until their database/APEX dependencies have been checked.
    languageId: markdown
